hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan in today's  video I'm going to answer a question  from one of my YouTube viewers  Kix who started a new clothing line and  one of my advice they wrote in saying hi  how're you doing I'm trying to start a  clothing company with my friend but a  budget is really low can you help kicks  so a couple of things for you kicks  starting the clothing line is definitely  capital intensive and you want to try to  make sure you're not spending a lot of  money until you're making money so my  advice to you is dream big have this big  vision if we want to go but start super  small and start going to customers who  you think have a need and get them to  place some orders before you're actually  spending any money and I know it's hard  cuz you don't have samples to go in and  show them and you're using you know  paper or using a computer or laptop to  show them designs but it's super  important to go out and get some orders  and make sure you're on the right track  before you start spending a lot of money  on different designs that flame out and  it happens all the time we spend a ton  of money creating your samples or create  an entire line and you produce it and  you try to sell it and nobody wants to  buy it and that's that's the problem you  want to avoid so you want to make sure  you're on the right track and you can  sell whatever you're going to make so go  and start talking to customers and get  them to place orders before you make  anything and make that a goal of your  business it's a lot tougher to get it  started but you're much more likely to  be successful because when you do launch  you'll have paying customers in hand  ready to buy from you the best way to do  this I think is go after the business  market and what I would try to do is  talk to companies who are local to you  you can get access to who are aggressive  on the marketing may be a little bit  edgy and could see working with you to  create something that could help promote  their business so I don't know what you  sell in the fashion business but said's  t-shirts I go and try to find a company  who again is it a little bit edgier it's  been a lot on marketing and offered to  create a custom t-shirt line for them  that can help expose their business to a  greater audience and that way when  you're doing with the business instead  of dealing with consumers a you have  somebody who is probably going to be  businessperson for you and they're  making much bigger orders so you might  sell 100 t-shirts you might sell a  thousand t-shirts and that's from one  customer instead of trying to make one  sale here one sale there to individual  consumers so it's a great way to get  cash flow positive start building money  into the business and then you can  expand it and later go after the  consumer market but I'd see if I could  start off going after the business  market the last thing I would do is also  try to model success so there's a ton of  fashion guys who've made it big started  from nothing and look at what they did  to be successful so again if your  t-shirts look at Johnny Cupcakes which  has an actual store look at Threadless  which is all online and see if there's  something that you can model from them  and other companies that you look up to  look how they got started how they make  extra money now doesn't really concern  you but how do they go from nothing to  those first few orders to you know  having a full-time business they can  support themselves off of those are some  lessons there that you can learn to help  great business so I hope that helps  kicks good luck sounds exciting if you  guys like the video please give it a  thumbs up and I'd also love to hear  feedback if you want to comment in the  video those comments help me determine  what new videos to make so I really look  forward to them that keeps me going so  please leave a comment and stay tuned  for the next episode  you
 

